quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  12,96,"When the bearer of good news arrived, he placed it (i.e. the shirt of Joseph) over his face, so he was immediately restored to sight. He said: ‘Did I not tell you that I know from Allah what you do not know?’"
  12,97,"They said: ‘Our father! Pray for the forgiveness of our sins. Indeed, we have been committing errors.’"
  12,98,"He said: ‘I shall seek forgiveness for you from my Lord. Indeed, He is the Most Forgiving, the All-Merciful.’"
  12,99,"So when they entered the presence of Yusuf, he drew his parents close to him and said: ‘Welcome to Egypt, you will all be safe here, if Allah wills!’"
  12,100,"He raised his parents to the throne, and they (all) fell before him in prostration. He said: ‘Father! This is the fulfilment of my dream, I had long ago, which my Lord has made come true. He was undoubtedly gracious to me when He brought me out of prison, and He brought you (here) from the desert after Satan had incited ill feelings between me and my brothers. Indeed, My Lord is Benevolent in what He wishes. Indeed, He is the All-Knowing, the All-Wise."
  12,101,My Lord! You have granted me a share of the kingdom and taught me the interpretation of dreams. Creator of the heavens and the earth! You are my Guardian in this world and in the Hereafter. Let me die in a state of total submission (to You) and join me with the righteous.’
  12,102,"(O Prophet!) These are the accounts of the Unseen, which We reveal to you. And you were not present with them when they conspired together and devised a plan (against Yusuf)."
  12,103,"Yet most people will not believe, no matter how eagerly you desire (for them)."
